<comment id="10448216" author="JIRAUSER52614" created="Mon, 8 Dec 2025 10:23:52 -0600"><p>Regarding, “<b>Provide File Requirements</b> - Bob to supply details on the control/count file format and coordinate with his technology team.”</p> <p> </p> <p>For the control information (effective date and record count).  We would request that the first record is the effective date, in the format of "HDR"|"YYYYMMDD"  and the last record is the record count of data records "TLR"|"0000000001"</p> <p>, excluding the first and last record (header/footer).  All data records would be pipe “|”  delimited and encapsulated with double quotes.  Include a  column record after the header effective date record.</p> <p>Example record from a different interface to gain an idea of the format:</p> <p>"HDR"|"20251110"                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           </p> <p>"Acct No"|"Uid No"|"Post Date"|"Tran Dte"|"Gl Acct"|"Gl Bank"|"Gl Cost Cntr"|"Intrchg Income"|"Fee Typ"|"Card Typ"|"Product Cde"|"Officer Nbr"|"Officer Nme"|"Custr Name"</p> <p>"200001"|"350"|"20251110"|"20251110"|"000004860430"|"0000123"|"000005923"|"  .18 "|"PI"|"ZPL"|"CCD"|"                    "|"                         "|"SMITH "</p> <p>"TLR"|"0000000001"</p> <p>Ravi Madhamanchi will provide the AWS S3 location at later time as it does involve development.  I will create a Jira story for the sprint from 12/1 to 12/12 to build the locations.  He can then pass that information to CPMS development for the MFS request.</p> <p> </p> <p>Thank you,</p></comment>
<comment id="10448215" author="JIRAUSER52614" created="Mon, 8 Dec 2025 10:23:48 -0600"><p>I added the information to the description, is this sufficient or please let me know if you have more questions that need to be answered.</p> <p> </p></comment>
