<customfield id="customfield_10300" key="com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.customfieldtypes:textarea">
<customfieldname>Acceptance Criteria</customfieldname>
<customfieldvalues>
<customfieldvalue><ul> <li>Develop SSIS package to generate the file in the required format.</li> <li>Create SQL objects to extract and transform data for the File with the Header and Footer Control Records. </li> <li>Create configuration parameters in SSISConfigurations needed for SSIS package including file name - LOC_Collateral.<b><font color="#de350b">txt</font></b></li> <li>Validate file structure and counts against specifications.</li> <li>provide a file drop location for CPMS file.</li> </ul> <ul> <li> </li> </ul> <p> </p> <p> </p> <ol> <li><b>Main</b> <b>Section of the File Fields</b> include: <ul> <li> <ul> <li><div class='table-wrap'> <table class='confluenceTable'><tbody> <tr> <td class='confluenceTd'><b>File Name</b></td> <td class='confluenceTd'><b>Fields Required</b></td> </tr> <tr> <td class='confluenceTd'>LOC_Collateral</td> <td class='confluenceTd'>1.<font color="#de350b">Pledge code</font><br/> 2."Checking Balance" <br/> 3."Savings Balance"<br/> 4.“Uninsured Balance” -  <br/> 5.“Collateral Required” - <br/> 6."Letter Of Credit Amount"  <br/> 7“Excess Collateral” - </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </li> </ul> </li> </ul> </li> </ol> <p> </p> <p>All data is at the pledge code level. </p> <p>Data resides in: <b>Letter of Credit Collateral Report</b></p> <p><b><span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="https://jira.us.bank-dns.com/secure/attachment/4138928/4138928_image-2025-12-08-09-35-30-200.png" height="114" width="370" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></b></p> <p> </p> <p>       <b>2. Control Records Fields Include</b></p> <p>For the control information (effective date and record count).  We would request that the first record is the effective date, in the format of "HDR"|"YYYYMMDD" and the last record is the record count of data records "TLR"|"0000000001"</p> <p>, excluding the first and last record (header/footer).  All data records would be pipe “|” delimited  and encapsulated with double quotes.  Include a column record after the header effective date record.</p> <p>Example record from a different interface to gain an idea of the format:</p> <p>"HDR"|"20251110"                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         </p> <p>"Acct No"|"Uid No"|"Post Date"|"Tran Dte"|"Gl Acct"|"Gl Bank"|"Gl Cost Cntr"|"Intrchg Income"|"Fee Typ"|"Card Typ"|"Product Cde"|"Officer Nbr"|"Officer Nme"|"Custr Name"</p> <p>"200001"|"350"|"20251110"|"20251110"|"000004860430"|"0000123"|"000005923"|"  .18 "|"PI"|"ZPL"|"CCD"|"                    "|"                         "|"SMITH "</p> <p>"TLR"|"0000000001"</p> <p>Note: The middle section in middle is of the different file. It is here to show the format field names would be different see section number 1 for actual field names</p> <p> </p> <p>Create new SSIS package in <a href="https://gitlab.us.bank-dns.com/CPMS_GITLAB/cpmsssis" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">https://gitlab.us.bank-dns.com/CPMS_GITLAB/cpmsssis</a> new SSIS project.  Use SSISConfigurations table in CPMS not in SystemsMaster.  </p> <p> </p></customfieldvalue>
